<%# A band across the page: its columns side by side on desktop, stacked below unless stack says on phones only or never (stack-*, site.css). The column count is the number of children, and columnWidths the share of each wherever they stand side by side (widths-*, tokens.css), equal when the section names no preset for that count; spaceBetween is the gap between the columns; spaceAbove and spaceBelow the space above and below them, or the theme's rhythm for the device when the style names none. A picture of the library (the props' picture) stands behind the columns, the section's first child, an img in a picture element: decorative, with the library's size, loaded at once for the first section of its document (first) and as it nears the view otherwise; its veil, the veil's strength and the point kept in view are data attributes (BlockStyle.picture_data) site.css draws. A picture the library no longer has draws nothing, and its settings no attribute. -%>
<%- style = block_style(block) -%>
<%- columns = Array(block["children"]).select { |child| child.is_a?(Hash) && child["type"] == "column" } -%>
<%- widths = BlockStyle.column_widths(block_props(block), columns.size) -%>
<%- stack = BlockStyle.stack(block_props(block), columns.size) -%>
<%- picture = section_picture(block_props(block), media) -%>
<%= tag.section(**block_root(block, [ "sec", BlockStyle.classes(style, "background"), BlockStyle.classes(style, "spaceAbove"), BlockStyle.classes(style, "spaceBelow"), BlockStyle.visibility_classes(style) ], data: { columns: columns.size, column_widths: widths, stack: stack, **BlockStyle.free_color_data(style, "background"), **(picture ? BlockStyle.picture_data(style) : {}) })) do %><%= tag.picture(tag.img(src: picture[0], width: picture[1], height: picture[2], alt: "", loading: block.equal?(local_assigns[:first]) ? "eager" : "lazy", decoding: "async"), class: "sw-picture") if picture %><%= tag.div(class: [ "sw-inner", "cols", "cols-#{columns.size.clamp(1, 4)}", ("widths-#{SiteTheme::TokenCss.class_value(widths)}" if widths), ("stack-#{stack}" if stack), BlockStyle.classes(style, "spaceBetween", family: "cols-gap") ]) do %><%= render_blocks(columns, allow: %w[column], media: media, content: local_assigns.fetch(:content, SiteContent::NONE), cached: local_assigns[:cached], answers: local_assigns[:answers]) %><% end %><% end %>
